-- 0040  The APIs the client designated on 6 October 2026, from their own
--       public specifications.
--
-- On 6 October the client asked every group to run the whole process with
-- thirteen named APIs. Ten of them were missing here or had no usable
-- schema; seven of those publish a usable specification, found and read on
-- 6 October. Each operation below was built with the
-- importer's own code -- detect, parseOpenApi3, toApiRow, extractDocumentSchemas,
-- toSchemaRows, toFieldRows, toParameterRows -- exactly as a Publisher import
-- would store it, then written here because the live importer refuses them:
-- Swagger 2.0 (Billit, Nanonets), more than 200 operations in one document
-- (Reckon One 577, Mailgun 258), operations it classifies as Other (B2Brouter
-- import, EzzyBills extraction, Nanonets OCR), and a document with no
-- e-invoicing terms (Mailgun). The category, network and a readable name are
-- set here by hand, following the client's taxonomy (extraction is a kind of
-- Transformation; Reckon One is a Transformation); the official name keeps the
-- document's own.
--
--   operation                                   source (sha256 of the document read on 6 Oct 2026)
--   AmitTransform Convert UBL JSON to UBL XML API
--       https://github.com/iamAmiK/invoice-conversion-api
--       sha256 b4262f95126565003725b2148a2d90f2deb15defce537abf45930178bddca22a
--       OpenAPI written from the provider's source code (frontend/public/specs/amittransform-openapi.json); called live on 6 Oct 2026.
--   Reckon One Create Invoice API
--       https://api-v2.reckonone.com/swagger/V2/swagger.json
--       sha256 3afa21d13bccec20b16db14f4e5eb95f2f03513994c7a055ad88851d79b9dfd4
--       Reckon One API v2 OpenAPI document.
--   Reckon One Get Invoice API
--       https://api-v2.reckonone.com/swagger/V2/swagger.json
--       sha256 3afa21d13bccec20b16db14f4e5eb95f2f03513994c7a055ad88851d79b9dfd4
--       Reckon One API v2 OpenAPI document.
--   Mailgun Send Message API
--       https://documentation.mailgun.com/_bundle/docs/mailgun/api-reference/send/mailgun.json?download
--       sha256 52608b7302fecbe482ba62cde5ab6ea2d505887366a3ea92156790eac70e6584
--       Mailgun Send API OpenAPI 3.1 document.
--   Billit Peppol Send Order API
--       https://api.billit.be/swagger/docs/v1
--       sha256 3a599ac6748350858047e064381d052fd37ea16aeaf97090acc6fb9f166bc194
--       Billit Swagger 2.0 document.
--   Nanonets OCR Extract From File API
--       https://app.nanonets.com/swagger
--       sha256 66205cdd9b25a1f5ec88258bdad149607139f1de9d078dd5acf15026cf8d64b6
--       Nanonets Swagger 2.0 document; its 200 response has an example but no schema, so the response schema was inferred from that example.
--   B2Brouter Import Invoice API
--       https://developer.b2brouter.net/reference/import-invoice
--       sha256 598d359688ad3c95022534f880be1c58773c5a131c235830bf4ffa3158560f21
--       OpenAPI definition embedded in the provider's reference page (import-invoice.md).
--   EzzyBills Upload Invoice Image API
--       https://apidocs.ezzydoc.com/mintlify/docs/ezzyrest/uploadinvoiceimage2
--       sha256 42f9ea862d32658447e7b1b8b1b34340043e072db9092ae061506b0aa2d0af30
--       OpenAPI definition embedded in the provider's reference page (uploadinvoiceimage2.md).
--   EzzyBills Get Extracted Invoice Data API
--       https://apidocs.ezzydoc.com/mintlify/docs/ezzyrest/getformdata
--       sha256 e8e9d6a594ed139cd1cac5e32929b1751c31fce2e6ada3afe8951c8f0b771a98
--       OpenAPI definition embedded in the provider's reference page (getformdata.md).
--
-- Notes
--   * AmitTransform has no published OpenAPI document; the group wrote one from
--     its source code and checked it against the running service.
--   * Nanonets documents its response only by example; the response schema is
--     inferred from that example and says so in its description.
--   * B2Brouter's document lists the staging server first; the endpoint is the
--     production host the composed API calls (a test_ key selects the sandbox).
--   * "Bilit" and "Nanoset" in the client's list are taken to be Billit and
--     Nanonets, by name and purpose.
--   * Upbrains, ECOSIO and Babelway publish no usable specification and are not
--     added; the client has been asked for them.
--
-- Records arrive as Published, as an import leaves them; an administrator
-- verifies them in the application.

-- --------------------------------------------------------------- format aliases

insert into public.format_alias (alias, canonical) values
  ('text/json', 'JSON'),
  ('application/*+json', 'JSON')
on conflict (alias) do nothing;

